<p>This visualization contextualizes the reward component of my analysis. By plotting the <em>adj_close</em> price, the resulting visual shows the actual wealth generated for stockholders over time (adjusted for all applicable splits and dividend distributions).</p>
<p>Readers should notice that while the Big Tech stock market sector is often referenced as a whole, the growth trajectories of companies within the sector are actually very different. A key observation is the difference in trend stability; some companies maintain a steady and reliable trend of capital appreciation, while other companies show much more fluctuation with massive vertical spikes followed by corrections*. This visualization shows that all tech stocks don’t behave the same way; it’s the specific stock, not the general sector, that determines whether investors experience consistent gains or extreme volatility over time.</p>
<p>*Note: Stock market corrections are generally defined as a drop in value of 10% or more from recent market highs.</p>
